---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout
  title="Real-Time Collaboration"
  description="Edit Varve documents together over a room you control: live cursors, cursor chat, spotlight follow, and undo that only reverses your own edits. App-hosted on your machine or self-hosted on your own server."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <main class="collab-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Real-Time Collaboration
      </nav>

      <header class="page-hero">
        <StatusPill status="beta" />
        <h1>Edit together, on a room you control.</h1>
        <p>
          Share a Varve document from the desktop app or your own room server.
          Changes replicate live; cursors, selections, and cursor chat show
          who is working where; and undo reverses only your own edits — never
          a collaborator's work. Your document stays local-first: joining a
          session never touches the file on your disk.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="collab-model site-card site-card--surface" aria-labelledby="collab-model-title">
        <h2 id="collab-model-title">Ordered semantic operations, not a merge lottery.</h2>
        <p>
          Every committed edit travels as a validated, property-level change
          list — the same semantic capture Varve's history records. The room
          host orders operations; every participant applies the same sequence,
          so documents converge without last-write-wins whole-document
          overwrites. A change that fails validation resynchronizes visibly
          instead of silently dropping.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="collab-pillars" aria-label="Collaboration capabilities">
        <div class="collab-pillar site-card">
          <h3>Undo that respects the room</h3>
          <p>
            In a shared session, undo reverses only what <em>you</em> did.
            If a teammate changed something after you, your undo skips it and
            says why instead of clobbering their work. Deleting restores from
            your own history; undoing a creation keeps the object if someone
            else has already built on it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="collab-pillar site-card">
          <h3>Presence that stays out of the way</h3>
          <p>
            Live cursors, remote selection outlines, and participant avatars
            are ephemeral by construction — they never enter your document,
            your history, or your saved files. Cursor chat opens with
            <kbd>/</kbd>, expires in seconds, and is never persisted anywhere.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="collab-pillar site-card">
          <h3>Spotlight, with consent</h3>
          <p>
            Spotlight your view to walk teammates through the canvas.
            Following is opt-in per person and any local camera interaction
            cancels it — nobody's viewport moves without their own say-so.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="collab-hosting site-card site-card--surface" aria-labelledby="collab-hosting-title">
        <h2 id="collab-hosting-title">Two hosting paths, one open implementation.</h2>
        <dl class="collab-hosting__paths">
          <div>
            <dt>Host on this device</dt>
            <dd>
              The desktop app runs a room server in-process on your machine.
              Sessions are reachable from other apps and browser tabs on the
              same computer — enough for pairing, review, and working across
              a browser and the desktop.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Self-host a room server</dt>
            <dd>
              Run the standalone room server (a single binary with durable
              storage) wherever you like and point Varve at it. You own the
              data, the retention, and the network; TLS terminates at your
              reverse proxy. No Varve-operated service sits in the middle.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p class="collab-hosting__note">
          Honest boundaries: cross-machine sessions need a server you can
          reach (LAN or internet with your own TLS), the host cannot read
          your documents without a room you created, and collaboration is
          not end-to-end encrypted — the room server stores documents in
          plaintext by design.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="collab-ctas" aria-label="Learn more">
        <a class="site-card" href={sitePath('/features/local-first')}>
          <h3>Why local-first matters</h3>
          <p>Your file is the authority; a session is replication, not a takeover.</p>
        </a>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .collab-page {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6, 32px);
    padding-block-end: var(--space-8, 48px);
  }

  .collab-model p,
  .collab-pillar p,
  .collab-hosting p {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .collab-pillars {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4, 16px);
  }

  .collab-pillar h3 {
    margin-block: 0 var(--space-2, 8px);
  }

  .collab-hosting__paths {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4, 16px);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3, 12px);
  }

  .collab-hosting__paths dt {
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-block-end: var(--space-1, 4px);
  }

  .collab-hosting__paths dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .collab-hosting__note {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .collab-ctas a {
    display: block;
    padding: var(--space-4, 16px);
  }

  .collab-ctas h3 {
    margin-block: 0 var(--space-1, 4px);
  }

  .collab-ctas p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  kbd {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-control-compact);
    padding: 0 0.35em;
    font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }
</style>
